# Quest Progress Contract
- GWToolboxpp is the Contract v1 producer; GuildWarsCodex is the consumer.
- The Contract is observational and does not authorize gameplay automation (no quest accept, reward claim, movement, or combat automation).
- Do not treat quest disappearance as confirmed completion.
- Preserve source and confidence; never collapse uncertain into confirmed.
- History is append-only; corrections supersede without erasing prior evidence.
- `producer.version` is metadata only and must not participate in event identity.
- Exporters must conform to the mirrored files in `docs/contracts/` (stable structured identity + SHA-256 fingerprint rules).
- Do not use runtime `std::hash` for portable Contract event fingerprints.
- Semantic Contract changes require synchronization with GuildWarsCodex before parser/exporter work proceeds.
